# Testing

The project runs locally with Docker Compose.

Always run the test suite inside the web container:

```bash
docker compose exec -e RAILS_ENV=test web bundle exec rspec
```

Do not run `bundle exec rspec` directly on the host.

Do not search for or start a host PostgreSQL server. PostgreSQL runs in the
Docker Compose `postgres` service.

For focused tests:

```bash
docker compose exec -e RAILS_ENV=test web bundle exec rspec spec/path/to/spec.rb
```

## After a branch is pushed / PR opened

When Grok Bot (or another agent) has already pushed the working branch to
GitHub and opened a PR, do **not** run the Docker Compose RSpec suite locally
to verify that work. CI/CD runs the tests on the PR; analyze the CI results
(checks on the PR) instead of re-running `docker compose exec … rspec` on the
host machine.

Local Docker RSpec remains the way to run tests while developing before push,
or when the user explicitly asks to run them locally.
